  "primary_subject_agency_ids": [],
  "summary": "EFF critiques Flock Safety's newly announced reforms \u2014 a default 7-day retention period, offense filtering for data-sharing, and enhanced audit tools \u2014 arguing they are cosmetic and reversible fixes to a fundamentally abusive mass surveillance system. The piece notes CEO Garrett Langley's shift in tone toward acknowledging critics and calls for legislation rather than vendor self-regulation.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The most consequential is Flock's default setting of an optional 7-day retention period for ALPR data, down from its original default optional 30-day retention period.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "He added that he has come to agree with groups like the American Civil Liberties Union and the Electronic Frontier Foundation that police should need an active case number to search Flock's data.",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    },
    {
      "quote": "We should not be letting companies decide how much privacy we deserve.",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    }
  ],
